by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":44,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The repaired network brings dev mean TTS down to **44.9 veh-h** (low 34.9 / nominal 45.3 / high 54.4), from 48.0 for the original with the failed detector. That is close to the 44.7 of the network with every detector working.\n\n**What I changed and why:** With W2 reading 0, the network never picked phase 3 unless the east pocket E2 had cars. In 2 of the 6 recorded episodes the junction deadlocked once traffic stopped arriving, with hidden W left-turners stuck. I fed the network a hand-set estimate of the two dead inputs, folded into the first layer:\n\n- the opposite pocket E2 (weight 0.8);\n- the queue on W1u, the upstream lane that feeds W2 (a queue there means W2 has overflowed);\n- a term that grows with green time, which acts as a timer to break deadlocks;\n- a phase-3 term so phase 3 can't stay stuck on.\n\nI also added a small timer so that one waiting N/S car eventually gets phase 0. The original network ignores a single car there.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 320 (b1 and four W1 columns).\n\n**Simulator calls:** all 5 used. Two early designs scored 45.2 but left 1–2 cars at the 30-minute cap in 2 of 9 episodes. Adding the fixes removed the leftovers (45.1). An E2 weight of 0.8 scored best; 1.0 scored 45.2.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.9, nominal 45.5, high 55.0. The high value is above the dev 54.4 because part of that result is probably seed luck.\n\nEverything is in `work/`; `NOTES.md` has the details and the risks I expect.","ttft_ms":2066,"type":"result","duration_ms":1025423,"uuid":"3f0d541a-3391-4f8a-8964-e2474928524a","ttft_stream_ms":1572,"time_to_request_ms":54,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":8,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":2,"m